From: Maximilian Kenfenheuer <maximilian.kenfenheuer@ksol.it>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:33:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdkfd: don't log expected userptr failures of file
 backed memory

ROCm registers host memory as KFD userptr with
AMDGPU_GEM_USERPTR_ANONONLY. For file backed mappings, e.g. a model file
mapped with mmap by llama.cpp, amdgpu_ttm_tt_get_user_pages() fails with
-EPERM and user space falls back to another way. Every such allocation
logged an error, hundreds per model load, flooding the kernel log and
the console.

Log -EPERM at debug level, other errors stay errors.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_amdkfd_gpuvm.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_amdkfd_gpuvm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_amdkfd_gpuvm.c
index d56728b..ddf5246 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_amdkfd_gpuvm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_amdkfd_gpuvm.c
@@ -1093,6 +1093,12 @@ static int init_user_pages(struct kgd_mem *mem, uint64_t user_addr,
 	if (ret) {
 		if (ret == -EAGAIN)
 			pr_debug("Failed to get user pages, try again\n");
+		else if (ret == -EPERM)
+			/* File backed memory with AMDGPU_GEM_USERPTR_ANONONLY,
+			 * user space falls back to another way to map it.
+			 */
+			pr_debug("%s: Failed to get user pages: %d\n",
+				 __func__, ret);
 		else
 			pr_err("%s: Failed to get user pages: %d\n", __func__, ret);
 		goto unregister_out;
-- 
